Project Title: Identifying VSR Function in Novel Genomes using Machine Learning

Project Description:
Developed machine learning models in Python (PyTorch, Scikit-Learn) to identify Viral Suppressors of 
RNA Silencing (VSRs) and assist the engineering of pathogen-resistant plants. Collected a balanced dataset 
of 300 viruses from UniProt and trained six distinct models including XGBoost, LightGBM, and SVM, while 
optimizing for overfitting. Achieved a peak predictive accuracy of 80% through hyperparameter tuning of 
a feed-forward neural network.
